WEBVTT

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.142 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.002 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:39.631 line:80%
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:41.008 line:80%
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:43.927 line:80%
[♪ soft nostalgic music playing]

00:00:44.011 --> 00:00:46.013 line:80%
[ice clinking, crackling]

00:00:49.099 --> 00:00:52.019 line:20%
EPISODE 1

00:00:53.771 --> 00:00:55.689 line:20%
[woman vocalizing tune over speaker phone]

00:00:55.773 --> 00:00:57.066 line:20%
[woman] <i>Hold on. Let me start over.</i>

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:01.528 line:20%
[woman continues vocalizing]

00:01:07.076 --> 00:01:08.535 line:20%
<i>The song that starts like that.</i>

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:13.248 line:20%
<i>I heard it a few days ago on the radio,</i>
<i>and they said it helps with insomnia.</i>

00:01:13.374 --> 00:01:15.376 line:20%
<i>You said your sleep pattern</i>
<i>has been off lately.</i>

00:01:15.459 --> 00:01:17.920 line:20%
<i>Try listening to it</i>
<i>when you can't sleep. Okay?</i>

00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:25.260 line:80%
<i>This is Seoul.</i>

00:01:25.344 --> 00:01:26.720 line:80%
<i>Boston, please respond.</i>

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.182 line:80%
<i>Hey, engineering student.</i>

00:01:32.851 --> 00:01:33.852 line:80%
<i>Chan.</i>

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.772 line:80%
<i>Hey, Chan!</i>

00:01:36.855 --> 00:01:38.857 line:80%
[♪ soft music continues]

00:01:54.498 --> 00:01:57.668 line:80%
[in English] Is it a gift?
I could engrave it if you'd like.

00:01:58.335 --> 00:01:59.753 line:80%
[sighs]

00:02:09.304 --> 00:02:11.974 line:80%
[team leader in Korean]
<i>The design contest winner is…</i>

00:02:12.474 --> 00:02:13.767 line:80%
Song Haran!

00:02:14.643 --> 00:02:16.437 line:80%
Me? You're kidding, right?

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.022 line:80%
Well, this is unexpected.

00:02:18.105 --> 00:02:19.523 line:80%
The second-year newbie won.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:20.899 line:80%
Congratulations, Haran.

00:02:20.983 --> 00:02:22.151 line:80%
-[woman 1] Congrats, newbie!
-Really?

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.069 line:80%
-[man] Congrats! You deserve it!
-[woman 2] Congratulations!

00:02:24.153 --> 00:02:25.821 line:80%
-[Haran] Thank you!
-[laptop pings]

00:02:25.904 --> 00:02:27.364 line:80%
I can't believe it!

00:02:27.448 --> 00:02:28.490 line:80%
<i>Chan! Chan! Chan!</i>

00:02:28.574 --> 00:02:29.908 line:80%
[laptop pings]

00:02:29.992 --> 00:02:31.994 line:80%
<i>The pen you sent me for my birthday…</i>

00:02:32.077 --> 00:02:35.748 line:80%
<i>I used it to draw a design,</i>
<i>and it won in our company contest!</i>

00:02:35.831 --> 00:02:38.667 line:80%
<i>-Let's go!</i>
-[Chan] It won?

00:02:38.751 --> 00:02:40.753 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Thank you so much!</i>

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.047 line:20%
<i>You know,</i>

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.465 line:80%
<i>you're my savior.</i>

00:02:56.393 --> 00:02:57.895 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:02:57.978 --> 00:02:59.063 line:80%
[phone chimes]

00:03:00.939 --> 00:03:02.232 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Hey, it smells like rain.</i>

00:03:02.316 --> 00:03:04.318 line:80%
[rain pattering]

00:03:15.329 --> 00:03:17.998 line:80%
<i>You know that particular smell</i>
<i>before it rains?</i>

00:03:18.082 --> 00:03:20.334 line:80%
<i>I love that smell.</i>

00:03:21.085 --> 00:03:24.588 line:80%
<i>But it disappears so quickly,</i>
<i>so I just stand there smelling it.</i>

00:03:25.381 --> 00:03:28.217 line:80%
[Chan] <i>That's the smell</i>
<i>of organic matter diffusing.</i>

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.385 line:80%
<i>It's called petrichor,</i>

00:03:29.468 --> 00:03:31.929 line:80%
<i>and it's when plant-derived</i>
<i>organic matter spreads--</i>

00:03:32.012 --> 00:03:34.431 line:80%
-[Haran] <i>Hey, nerd. Stop.</i>
-[Chan] <i>The pores in rock crevices…</i>

00:03:35.724 --> 00:03:38.811 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Stop ruining my joy</i>
<i>with science talk, you nerd.</i>

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:42.481 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:03:42.564 --> 00:03:45.275 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Anyway, smelling the rain</i>
<i>puts me in a good mood.</i>

00:03:45.943 --> 00:03:48.278 line:80%
<i>You should try it sometime.</i>
<i>I recommend it.</i>

00:03:53.492 --> 00:03:57.955 line:80%
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

00:04:36.994 --> 00:04:40.497 line:80%
[Haran] <i>But the catch is that</i>
<i>you always end up with a nasty cold.</i>

00:04:44.877 --> 00:04:46.545 line:80%
ACHOO!

00:04:46.879 --> 00:04:47.880 line:80%
[inhales deeply]

00:04:49.048 --> 00:04:50.049 line:80%
[sneezes]

00:04:50.591 --> 00:04:51.842 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:04:52.718 --> 00:04:53.719 line:80%
[sneezes]

00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:00.893 line:80%
Hey, it's a vapor trail.

00:05:01.477 --> 00:05:04.480 line:80%
[groans] I wish I could get on a plane
and go see Chan.

00:05:05.439 --> 00:05:07.316 line:80%
The boyfriend who's studying in Boston?

00:05:07.399 --> 00:05:10.527 line:80%
I heard Chan's too busy with research
to come during vacation.

00:05:10.611 --> 00:05:12.655 line:80%
Eunchan, you know Haran's boyfriend?

00:05:12.738 --> 00:05:13.739 line:80%
A bit.

00:05:13.822 --> 00:05:14.948 line:80%
He's my little brother.

00:05:15.032 --> 00:05:16.909 line:80%
-What?
-Really?

00:05:16.992 --> 00:05:20.829 line:80%
Let's enjoy our four days off
and work hard for our next season.

00:05:20.913 --> 00:05:22.164 line:80%
[employees] Yes, ma'am!

00:05:22.247 --> 00:05:23.248 line:80%
[employees laugh]

00:05:24.249 --> 00:05:25.250 line:80%
Four days?

00:05:26.418 --> 00:05:28.587 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:05:28.671 --> 00:05:29.838 line:80%
[Haran panting] Hey, Yujeong!

00:05:29.922 --> 00:05:31.632 line:80%
[Yujeong] <i>We're getting together later.</i>
<i>You free?</i>

00:05:32.216 --> 00:05:33.467 line:80%
<i>Why are you running?</i>

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:36.428 line:80%
I'm going to Boston to meet Chan.

00:05:36.929 --> 00:05:38.514 line:80%
I'll tell you everything later.

00:05:39.556 --> 00:05:40.557 line:80%
[phone beeps]

00:05:41.809 --> 00:05:43.811 line:80%
[birds chirping]

00:05:53.153 --> 00:05:54.697 line:80%
[sighs]

00:06:02.663 --> 00:06:03.664 line:80%
[sighs]

00:06:11.964 --> 00:06:13.298 line:80%
[laptop pings]

00:06:16.552 --> 00:06:17.553 line:80%
Tsk.

00:06:18.137 --> 00:06:19.221 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:06:21.724 --> 00:06:24.059 line:20%
[Haran] <i>Chan, I saw a vapor trail earlier.</i>

00:06:24.143 --> 00:06:26.645 line:20%
<i>But that made me want</i>
<i>to get on a plane to go see you.</i>

00:06:26.729 --> 00:06:27.980 line:20%
<i>So…</i>

00:06:28.772 --> 00:06:32.151 line:20%
<i>-Ta-da! I'm at the airport!</i>
-[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:33.485 line:80%
Isn't that crazy?

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:35.904 line:80%
I'll have to come back
after only a few hours,

00:06:35.988 --> 00:06:38.115 line:80%
but I wanted
to tell you something in person.

00:06:38.824 --> 00:06:42.411 line:80%
<i>I'll be there at about 1:00 p.m.</i>
<i>in Boston, so just hang in there.</i>

00:06:42.911 --> 00:06:43.912 line:80%
<i>Wait.</i>

00:06:44.663 --> 00:06:47.750 line:20%
<i>I changed my mind.</i>
<i>I'm going to say it now. Hang on.</i>

00:06:50.586 --> 00:06:51.962 line:80%
Chan.

00:06:52.046 --> 00:06:53.380 line:80%
I love you.

00:06:54.631 --> 00:06:56.258 line:80%
I love you, Chan. [chuckles]

00:07:03.766 --> 00:07:05.893 line:80%
[ticking]

00:07:16.612 --> 00:07:17.613 line:80%
[in English] BIT, please.

00:07:30.959 --> 00:07:32.961 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music continues]

00:07:38.634 --> 00:07:40.219 line:80%
5 MINUTES, 0.7 MILES

00:07:40.302 --> 00:07:42.012 line:80%
[gasps, in Korean] Just five minutes left.

00:08:10.833 --> 00:08:11.834 line:80%
[student in English] Hey!

00:08:17.256 --> 00:08:18.549 line:80%
[panting]

00:08:22.553 --> 00:08:24.471 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music playing]

00:08:31.854 --> 00:08:32.896 line:80%
[sighs]

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.573 line:80%
[explosion]

00:08:45.826 --> 00:08:47.536 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:08:47.619 --> 00:08:48.787 line:80%
[distant explosion]

00:08:53.834 --> 00:08:55.461 line:80%
[sirens wailing, blaring]

00:08:57.463 --> 00:08:59.465 line:80%
[people clamoring]

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.686 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.564 line:80%
EUNCHAN

00:09:15.648 --> 00:09:16.690 line:80%
[gasps]

00:09:18.025 --> 00:09:19.443 line:80%
Hello?

00:09:19.526 --> 00:09:22.196 line:80%
[Eunchan] <i>Haran, what do I do?</i>

00:09:25.658 --> 00:09:26.784 line:80%
<i>Chan…</i>

00:09:28.035 --> 00:09:29.703 line:80%
[sobbing] <i>Chan is…</i>

00:09:29.787 --> 00:09:31.789 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music continues]

00:09:59.775 --> 00:10:00.776 line:80%
[shuddering]

00:10:00.859 --> 00:10:02.861 line:80%
[high-pitched ringing]

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:06.323 line:80%
[groans softly]

00:10:11.245 --> 00:10:12.246 line:80%
[exhales]

00:10:15.249 --> 00:10:18.085 line:80%
-[sirens wailing, blaring]
-[people clamoring]

00:10:18.168 --> 00:10:20.921 line:80%
[♪ somber music playing]

00:10:53.495 --> 00:10:55.873 line:80%
[♪ somber music continuing]

00:11:15.934 --> 00:11:19.188 line:20%
SEOUL, SEVEN YEARS LATER

00:11:19.688 --> 00:11:20.689 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:11:20.773 --> 00:11:22.775 line:80%
[♪ upbeat electronic music
playing on speakers]

00:11:26.362 --> 00:11:27.363 line:80%
Let's begin.

00:11:28.113 --> 00:11:29.114 line:80%
One, two, three.

00:11:29.573 --> 00:11:30.658 line:80%
[cameras clicking]

00:11:30.741 --> 00:11:32.159 line:80%
Awesome.

00:11:32.242 --> 00:11:34.161 line:80%
-[Hayeong] All right.
-Let's take a few more and call it.

00:11:34.244 --> 00:11:35.287 line:80%
Okay.

00:11:48.425 --> 00:11:50.177 line:80%
Excuse me. Coming through.

00:11:54.348 --> 00:11:56.433 line:80%
-Hi.
-Hey. The outfits…

00:11:56.517 --> 00:11:58.519 line:80%
I like how the texture shows here.

00:11:58.602 --> 00:12:00.604 line:80%
[♪ upbeat music continuing]

00:12:04.566 --> 00:12:06.568 line:80%
[cameras clicking]

00:12:06.652 --> 00:12:07.736 line:80%
Nice.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.697 line:80%
-Nice! You look great.
-[cameraman] Perfect.

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:11.949 line:80%
Dart. 0.5.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.580 line:80%
Ms. Kim is here.

00:12:18.998 --> 00:12:19.999 line:80%
[hiccups]

00:12:29.299 --> 00:12:32.177 line:80%
Let's fix the darts by 0.5 inches
before resuming.

00:12:32.261 --> 00:12:34.054 line:80%
Start pinning right away!

00:12:37.725 --> 00:12:38.892 line:80%
Lights.

00:12:40.436 --> 00:12:43.731 line:80%
Dim the backlight by 10%
and adjust the fill lights.

00:12:43.814 --> 00:12:44.898 line:80%
Everyone, move.

00:12:45.524 --> 00:12:47.484 line:80%
-[staff 1] All right.
-[staff 2] Hurry!

00:12:48.777 --> 00:12:49.903 line:80%
Quickly, everyone!

00:12:52.573 --> 00:12:53.741 line:80%
[camera clicking]

00:12:53.824 --> 00:12:54.825 line:80%
All right.

00:12:55.701 --> 00:12:56.744 line:80%
Two, three.

00:12:58.245 --> 00:12:59.246 line:80%
[in English] Okay.

00:13:00.205 --> 00:13:02.333 line:80%
[in Korean] Okay. Great work, everyone.

00:13:02.416 --> 00:13:04.084 line:80%
-Great work, everyone.
-[applause]

00:13:05.878 --> 00:13:08.380 line:80%
The Korean queen of fashion,

00:13:09.048 --> 00:13:11.133 line:80%
the head of Nana Atelier.

00:13:11.216 --> 00:13:13.218 line:80%
Give a round of applause
to our queen, Nana.

00:13:13.302 --> 00:13:14.553 line:80%
[Nana] It's fine.

00:13:14.636 --> 00:13:16.472 line:80%
Clap for the person in charge, not me.

00:13:16.555 --> 00:13:20.059 line:80%
Ah, the person who oversaw it all,
from the outfits to the shoot.

00:13:20.142 --> 00:13:22.770 line:80%
Let's give a hand
to our lead designer, Song Haran!

00:13:22.853 --> 00:13:25.272 line:80%
[employees cheering, applauding]

00:13:28.484 --> 00:13:29.735 line:80%
Excuse me…

00:13:29.818 --> 00:13:32.363 line:80%
I'm sorry, but I don't think she's here.
[chuckles nervously]

00:13:33.155 --> 00:13:34.239 line:80%
[staff] Where did she go?

00:13:35.407 --> 00:13:36.700 line:80%
-She's not here?
-[exclaims]

00:13:36.784 --> 00:13:37.785 line:80%
What's going on?

00:13:37.868 --> 00:13:38.869 line:80%
She was just here.

00:13:39.703 --> 00:13:42.373 line:80%
She even approved the final select shots.

00:13:42.915 --> 00:13:43.916 line:80%
Ghosting…

00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:47.419 line:80%
[groans] She disappeared again,
like always.

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:49.463 line:80%
[cell phone chimes]

00:13:49.546 --> 00:13:52.591 line:80%
Ms. Song's routine never changes.
[chuckles]

00:13:52.675 --> 00:13:53.967 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:13:54.051 --> 00:13:56.762 line:80%
She's like my salary.

00:13:56.845 --> 00:13:58.055 line:80%
She disappears every time.

00:13:58.597 --> 00:14:00.391 line:80%
[Seung-gyu] Right. [chuckles]

00:14:00.474 --> 00:14:02.476 line:80%
[silence]

00:14:11.402 --> 00:14:15.572 line:80%
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

00:14:28.669 --> 00:14:29.753 line:80%
[sighs]

00:15:08.167 --> 00:15:09.752 line:80%
[indistinct announcement on PA]

00:15:11.462 --> 00:15:13.422 line:80%
Mr. Yeon's coming to our hotel.

00:15:13.505 --> 00:15:15.591 line:80%
The car rental…

00:15:16.842 --> 00:15:17.843 line:80%
Where did he go?

00:15:20.137 --> 00:15:22.222 line:80%
[sighs] Did he wander off again?

00:15:25.309 --> 00:15:27.561 line:80%
[man in English]
Do you guys remember what I just told you?

00:15:27.645 --> 00:15:28.729 line:80%
[group] Yeah!

00:15:28.812 --> 00:15:30.689 line:80%
-[man] Okay, let's go.
-[camera whirs]

00:15:31.357 --> 00:15:33.067 line:80%
[camera ticking]

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:34.902 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:15:36.278 --> 00:15:37.655 line:80%
[in Korean] What's one plus one?

00:15:37.738 --> 00:15:40.658 line:80%
-[group] Two!
-[in English] Two!

00:15:40.991 --> 00:15:42.034 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:15:42.117 --> 00:15:43.118 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:15:43.202 --> 00:15:44.912 line:80%
[Chan in Korean] Ben, look.
Didn't it come out nice?

00:15:45.746 --> 00:15:48.207 line:80%
[scoffs] I bet
you're the only one in this world

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:52.378 line:80%
who always makes friends
with everyone on the plane.

00:15:52.461 --> 00:15:53.754 line:80%
You think so?

00:15:56.632 --> 00:15:59.218 line:80%
Mm! [exclaims]
This taste brings back memories.

00:15:59.301 --> 00:16:00.386 line:80%
[exclaims]

00:16:01.845 --> 00:16:03.472 line:80%
When was the last time you were in Korea?

00:16:04.056 --> 00:16:06.141 line:80%
[inhales sharply]
It's been about seven years.

00:16:06.225 --> 00:16:08.310 line:80%
[Ben] Isn't your family in Korea?

00:16:08.394 --> 00:16:09.770 line:80%
Why didn't you come--

00:16:09.853 --> 00:16:12.189 line:80%
Ben. Let's go to Hangang River
after the meeting.

00:16:12.272 --> 00:16:15.192 line:80%
-[laughs]
-No, wait. Maybe Namsan?

00:16:15.275 --> 00:16:16.276 line:80%
Oh!

00:16:16.902 --> 00:16:18.904 line:80%
[in English] I got a list, man.

00:16:19.905 --> 00:16:24.743 line:80%
[in Korean] Okay. Let's look through
my Seoul destinations list.

00:16:25.369 --> 00:16:26.745 line:80%
-First…
-[exclaiming]

00:16:26.829 --> 00:16:28.580 line:80%
No, I can't hear you! I'm going to sleep.

00:16:28.664 --> 00:16:29.957 line:80%
[exclaiming]

00:16:30.541 --> 00:16:32.001 line:80%
Then, I'll have fun by myself.

00:16:32.084 --> 00:16:33.961 line:80%
-Great. Go do that.
-[chuckles]

00:16:35.337 --> 00:16:38.048 line:80%
[breathes deeply]

00:16:41.552 --> 00:16:44.054 line:80%
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:16:44.138 --> 00:16:45.681 line:80%
I really did come back.

00:16:48.309 --> 00:16:49.351 line:80%
[window whirring]

00:16:50.686 --> 00:16:51.854 line:80%
[wind whooshing]

00:17:09.705 --> 00:17:11.623 line:80%
[wind whooshing]

00:17:11.707 --> 00:17:13.792 line:80%
-[leaves rustling]
-[birds chirping]

00:17:13.876 --> 00:17:16.628 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:17:17.338 --> 00:17:19.381 line:80%
Nice to meet you. I'm Yeon Taeseok.

00:17:19.465 --> 00:17:21.508 line:80%
[exclaims] It's nice to meet you,
Mr. Yeon!

00:17:21.592 --> 00:17:23.427 line:80%
I really wanted to see you.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:25.304 line:80%
After communicating through just emails,

00:17:25.387 --> 00:17:26.513 line:80%
I knew I'd be happy,

00:17:26.597 --> 00:17:28.515 line:80%
but I can't believe how excited I am.

00:17:28.599 --> 00:17:31.352 line:80%
-Well, I'm not that excited…
-[♪ happy music playing]

00:17:31.435 --> 00:17:33.270 line:80%
Just think of him

00:17:33.354 --> 00:17:35.773 line:80%
like a golden retriever
who loves people. [chuckles]

00:17:35.856 --> 00:17:37.691 line:80%
I see. A golden retriever.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:39.735 line:80%
But your Korean is really…

00:17:39.818 --> 00:17:41.528 line:80%
Ah. I'm Ben.

00:17:41.612 --> 00:17:44.948 line:80%
My wife's Korean,
and my in-laws live in Pangyo.

00:17:45.032 --> 00:17:46.825 line:80%
-Ah. Right. Ben.
-[Ben] Yes.

00:17:46.909 --> 00:17:48.035 line:80%
[claps]

00:17:48.118 --> 00:17:50.287 line:80%
Stand over here, Ben.

00:17:50.371 --> 00:17:51.664 line:80%
Let me formally introduce myself.

00:17:52.456 --> 00:17:54.083 line:80%
I'm the one who proposed this project

00:17:54.833 --> 00:17:57.503 line:80%
and a supervisor
with CAN Animation Studio, Seon…

00:17:58.879 --> 00:18:03.384 line:80%
Well, many people get confused,
so let me tell you in advance.

00:18:03.467 --> 00:18:05.844 line:80%
My name's Seonu Chan, not Seon Uchan.

00:18:07.179 --> 00:18:08.764 line:80%
-[Remy] This too?
-[Hayeong] Mmm-hmm.

00:18:09.473 --> 00:18:11.809 line:80%
Wait. Hang on. I can't carry this alone.

00:18:11.892 --> 00:18:13.435 line:80%
[in English] You can do it, baby.

00:18:13.519 --> 00:18:16.355 line:80%
-[staff 1 in Korean] Great work, guys.
-[staff 2] Great job.

00:18:16.438 --> 00:18:19.149 line:80%
-[staff 3] Great work, everyone.
-[staff 4] Good job.

00:18:19.233 --> 00:18:22.152 line:80%
After checking if we have everything,
let's clean up and go.

00:18:22.236 --> 00:18:24.989 line:80%
We should go now
if we want to make it to the afterparty.

00:18:25.072 --> 00:18:26.073 line:80%
[Sol] What's going on?

00:18:26.782 --> 00:18:29.284 line:80%
I guess Ms. Song didn't arrive first.

00:18:29.368 --> 00:18:31.662 line:80%
-I should text her to come to the party.
-[Remy in English] Stop!

00:18:31.745 --> 00:18:33.831 line:80%
[in Korean] Sol, our rookie intern.

00:18:34.456 --> 00:18:35.916 line:80%
You're still clueless about her.

00:18:36.709 --> 00:18:39.962 line:80%
Honey, have you ever had lunch
with Ms. Song before?

00:18:40.045 --> 00:18:42.339 line:80%
-Yes or no?
-No, never.

00:18:43.048 --> 00:18:46.802 line:80%
She always leaves first during lunchtime,
so she must be busy meeting people.

00:18:46.885 --> 00:18:50.139 line:80%
-Not at all.
-Every day, all the time.

00:18:50.222 --> 00:18:52.891 line:80%
Do you think it makes sense
to always have plans?

00:18:52.975 --> 00:18:56.520 line:80%
Gosh. Are you saying
she's avoiding us on purpose?

00:18:56.603 --> 00:18:58.272 line:80%
That's right. [chuckles]

00:18:58.355 --> 00:19:01.692 line:80%
She loves to brood on her own.

00:19:01.775 --> 00:19:03.485 line:80%
She really isn't my vibe.

00:19:03.569 --> 00:19:06.739 line:80%
[sighs] Where is she
always disappearing to?

00:19:10.868 --> 00:19:13.162 line:80%
[♪ serene music playing on speakers]

00:19:17.791 --> 00:19:19.293 line:80%
[sighs contentedly]

00:19:23.881 --> 00:19:25.507 line:80%
PARK GENIUS

00:19:50.991 --> 00:19:53.577 line:80%
-[automation in English] <i>Two points.</i>
-[exclaims]

00:19:53.952 --> 00:19:54.953 line:80%
<i>Three points.</i>

00:19:55.037 --> 00:19:56.163 line:80%
[game buzzes]

00:19:56.246 --> 00:19:57.247 line:80%
<i>-Three points.</i>
-[exclaims]

00:19:57.331 --> 00:19:58.832 line:80%
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]
-[arcade sounds]

00:19:58.916 --> 00:20:00.000 line:80%
[exclaims]

00:20:00.084 --> 00:20:01.168 line:80%
-[camera clicks]
-[in Korean] I got it!

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:06.632 line:80%
It looks so good.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:08.884 line:80%
Mmm.

00:20:10.511 --> 00:20:12.012 line:80%
CHAN SENT PHOTOS

00:20:12.096 --> 00:20:14.223 line:80%
-[cell phone pinging]
-[groans]

00:20:14.306 --> 00:20:16.809 line:80%
[sighing]

00:20:17.893 --> 00:20:18.936 line:80%
[pinging stops]

00:20:23.357 --> 00:20:25.025 line:80%
[in English] Oh, God.

00:20:25.109 --> 00:20:26.276 line:80%
[sighs]

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:29.113 line:80%
[in Korean] What sort of Korean
enjoys Korea this much?

00:20:29.905 --> 00:20:31.657 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music continues]

00:20:33.701 --> 00:20:34.785 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:20:48.882 --> 00:20:50.884 line:80%
[♪ serene music playing on speakers]

00:20:53.595 --> 00:20:55.264 line:80%
[machine thudding loudly]

00:21:04.606 --> 00:21:05.941 line:80%
Sorry about that.

00:21:06.859 --> 00:21:10.362 line:80%
The ice machine
is acting up today. [chuckles]

00:21:10.863 --> 00:21:12.031 line:80%
Be quiet.

00:21:14.533 --> 00:21:15.534 line:80%
Quiet!

00:21:17.119 --> 00:21:19.288 line:80%
Good boy. [chuckles]

00:21:19.371 --> 00:21:20.664 line:80%
This is AI.

00:21:21.457 --> 00:21:22.708 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:21:23.792 --> 00:21:24.918 line:80%
Oh, those.

00:21:25.002 --> 00:21:27.046 line:80%
If you're interested, check them out.

00:21:27.129 --> 00:21:30.090 line:80%
One of my regulars here
organized an exhibit,

00:21:30.174 --> 00:21:33.552 line:80%
and they're showing paintings
for each season.

00:21:33.635 --> 00:21:36.305 line:80%
You can take a bunch of those
and go with friends.

00:21:36.388 --> 00:21:39.016 line:80%
One is enough. Thank you.

00:21:39.099 --> 00:21:40.726 line:80%
Ah. Really?

00:21:42.978 --> 00:21:44.855 line:80%
Going by yourself will be nice, too.

00:21:46.774 --> 00:21:49.943 line:20%
RADIANT SEASONS

00:21:50.027 --> 00:21:51.612 line:20%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:21:53.572 --> 00:21:56.408 line:80%
[receptionist] Proceed through
the four seasonal rooms in order.

00:21:56.492 --> 00:21:57.493 line:80%
Okay.

00:21:59.703 --> 00:22:02.748 line:80%
"SHIM"
Coffee House

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:07.169 line:20%
SPRING ROOM, THE WONDER OF LIFE

00:22:22.101 --> 00:22:24.687 line:20%
WINTER ROOM, DEEP SILENCE

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:25.771 line:80%
[music fades]

00:22:30.943 --> 00:22:32.861 line:80%
[footsteps]

00:22:39.076 --> 00:22:40.119 line:80%
[clicks]

00:22:41.996 --> 00:22:42.997 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:22:48.711 --> 00:22:49.712 line:80%
[clicks]

00:22:53.632 --> 00:22:55.050 line:80%
[guide on headphones] <i>A lone woman</i>

00:22:55.134 --> 00:22:58.137 line:80%
<i>stands with her back turned</i>
<i>in a white, snowy landscape,</i>

00:22:58.887 --> 00:23:01.890 line:80%
<i>quietly conveying</i>
<i>a sense of sorrow and emptiness.</i>

00:23:04.268 --> 00:23:06.854 line:80%
<i>Rather than sharp tension,</i>
<i>the artist's brush captures</i>

00:23:07.563 --> 00:23:11.066 line:80%
<i>the gentle air</i>
<i>and subtle tremble of light.</i>

00:23:11.150 --> 00:23:13.152 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

00:23:20.242 --> 00:23:23.037 line:80%
No way…

00:23:50.981 --> 00:23:51.982 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Chan.</i>

00:23:52.733 --> 00:23:53.901 line:80%
<i>I love you, Chan.</i>

00:23:55.486 --> 00:23:57.946 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song continuing]

00:24:06.205 --> 00:24:07.206 line:80%
[Chan exclaims]

00:24:09.249 --> 00:24:10.250 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:24:22.971 --> 00:24:24.932 line:80%
[panting]

00:24:31.522 --> 00:24:33.941 line:80%
You idiot.
What will you do if it really is her?

00:24:37.486 --> 00:24:38.487 line:80%
[song fades]

00:24:40.322 --> 00:24:42.324 line:80%
[♪ soft surreal music playing]

00:25:06.223 --> 00:25:07.224 line:80%
[music fades]

00:25:09.268 --> 00:25:10.936 line:80%
[hammering echoes]

00:25:11.020 --> 00:25:13.605 line:80%
[saw whirring]

00:25:15.607 --> 00:25:18.110 line:80%
-[rattling]
-[♪ tense music playing]

00:25:18.193 --> 00:25:19.862 line:80%
-[wood clanks]
-Huh?

00:25:21.947 --> 00:25:23.198 line:80%
Hey, watch out.

00:25:26.618 --> 00:25:28.203 line:80%
-[metal creaks]
-Watch out!

00:25:29.413 --> 00:25:30.831 line:80%
Song Haran!

00:25:36.879 --> 00:25:38.839 line:80%
-[crashing]
-[women scream]

00:25:41.842 --> 00:25:44.428 line:80%
-[exclaims] Are you okay?
-[frantic chatter]

00:25:44.511 --> 00:25:45.679 line:80%
That was close.

00:25:45.763 --> 00:25:47.389 line:80%
-Are you all right?
-[women gasp]

00:25:47.473 --> 00:25:49.433 line:80%
-[woman] Gosh. That was close.
-[breathing shakily]

00:25:49.516 --> 00:25:51.101 line:80%
[man] Are you okay?

00:25:51.185 --> 00:25:53.228 line:80%
[woman] Should we call emergency services?

00:25:53.312 --> 00:25:54.563 line:80%
[man] Are you all right?

00:25:54.647 --> 00:25:55.981 line:80%
-[woman] Are you okay?
-[man] Are you okay?

00:25:56.065 --> 00:25:57.733 line:80%
-Come quickly!
-[Haran] Yes, I'm okay.

00:25:57.816 --> 00:25:59.068 line:80%
-[woman] Are you okay?
-[man] Is anyone hurt?

00:25:59.151 --> 00:26:00.527 line:80%
[man 2] Get down here!

00:26:00.611 --> 00:26:02.029 line:80%
-[man 1] Are they okay?
-[man 2] It's dangerous.

00:26:02.112 --> 00:26:03.280 line:80%
You should all come down.

00:26:03.364 --> 00:26:04.823 line:80%
-[woman] That was so close.
-[man] Come on.

00:26:06.283 --> 00:26:08.285 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:26:09.453 --> 00:26:11.038 line:80%
[Ben on phone] <i>Hey, Too Much.</i>

00:26:11.121 --> 00:26:14.083 line:80%
<i>Why is a Korean so busy touring Seoul?</i>

00:26:14.166 --> 00:26:15.209 line:80%
Right?

00:26:15.876 --> 00:26:17.795 line:80%
Maybe I overdid it.

00:26:19.588 --> 00:26:21.799 line:80%
I fled seven years ago

00:26:23.008 --> 00:26:25.719 line:80%
because I thought I'd see her
everywhere I went.

00:26:26.679 --> 00:26:28.847 line:80%
Seoul seems so big,

00:26:29.515 --> 00:26:32.226 line:80%
but it was actually really small.

00:26:32.309 --> 00:26:34.103 line:80%
Are you saying it's big or small?

00:26:35.896 --> 00:26:36.897 line:80%
Hey, Chan.

00:26:38.107 --> 00:26:39.608 line:80%
<i>Did something happen?</i>

00:26:40.818 --> 00:26:42.277 line:80%
Mmm…

00:26:45.114 --> 00:26:47.116 line:80%
Something did happen…

00:26:47.992 --> 00:26:48.993 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:26:50.619 --> 00:26:52.329 line:80%
but I'm going to pretend it didn't.

00:26:53.831 --> 00:26:57.042 line:80%
I'll think about this today
and forget about it tomorrow,

00:26:57.126 --> 00:26:59.378 line:80%
so don't worry and go to bed.

00:26:59.461 --> 00:27:00.587 line:80%
Bye.

00:27:01.755 --> 00:27:03.340 line:80%
[phone clicks, beeps]

00:27:06.552 --> 00:27:07.553 line:80%
[smacks lips]

00:27:11.974 --> 00:27:13.058 line:80%
[sighs]

00:27:14.393 --> 00:27:15.602 line:80%
[pen scratching]

00:27:21.692 --> 00:27:24.320 line:80%
RADIANT SEASONS

00:27:24.403 --> 00:27:26.572 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music playing]

00:27:26.655 --> 00:27:27.656 line:80%
[Chan] Song Haran!

00:27:28.615 --> 00:27:30.242 line:80%
-[crashes]
-[women scream]

00:27:31.785 --> 00:27:34.121 line:80%
I'm sure they called my name.

00:27:35.497 --> 00:27:36.623 line:80%
Who was it?

00:27:39.460 --> 00:27:43.797 line:80%
Of the three, I'm in charge of designing
and planning the Korean character… [sighs]

00:27:43.881 --> 00:27:45.591 line:80%
CHARACTERS
NIA, WON, FIN

00:27:45.674 --> 00:27:49.386 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Just think of me
as the guy in charge of Won.

00:27:50.220 --> 00:27:52.514 line:80%
[Ben] To highlight the identities
of each character,

00:27:52.598 --> 00:27:55.768 line:80%
we planned collaborations
with designers from each country.

00:27:56.352 --> 00:27:58.103 line:80%
[Chan] I made the collaboration offer

00:27:58.187 --> 00:28:02.650 line:80%
because I really wanted you
to design the Korean character's outfits.

00:28:03.984 --> 00:28:05.235 line:80%
What do you think, Ms. Kim?

00:28:10.783 --> 00:28:11.784 line:80%
Ms. Kim?

00:28:14.286 --> 00:28:16.747 line:80%
So why should I do this?

00:28:18.123 --> 00:28:19.416 line:80%
[Chan] I was curious.

00:28:19.958 --> 00:28:22.711 line:80%
To be honest, I was excited.

00:28:22.795 --> 00:28:26.048 line:80%
I thought your roots
were similar to Won's.

00:28:26.924 --> 00:28:30.594 line:80%
Won isn't someone who shines like the sun.

00:28:30.678 --> 00:28:33.597 line:80%
Instead, she gives light

00:28:33.681 --> 00:28:35.683 line:80%
to those in the darkness,

00:28:36.558 --> 00:28:37.559 line:80%
like the moon.

00:28:38.185 --> 00:28:39.853 line:80%
<i>"Douceur lunaire."</i>

00:28:40.604 --> 00:28:42.606 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:28:43.232 --> 00:28:44.233 line:80%
[mouthing] What's that?

00:28:45.317 --> 00:28:46.860 line:80%
"Soft moonlight."

00:28:46.944 --> 00:28:49.488 line:80%
The first collection you put out
when you were 22.

00:28:49.571 --> 00:28:51.073 line:80%
I saw it myself.

00:28:52.199 --> 00:28:55.828 line:80%
You reinterpreted Korean traditional silk
through moonlight.

00:28:57.788 --> 00:28:59.999 line:80%
You saw it yourself?

00:29:00.082 --> 00:29:02.918 line:80%
It was on display at the fashion school
you attended in France.

00:29:04.503 --> 00:29:06.588 line:80%
Thanks to you,

00:29:07.881 --> 00:29:09.591 line:80%
I got to see the Eiffel Tower, too.

00:29:12.761 --> 00:29:16.890 line:80%
So, what if you expressed Won
with roots like that?

00:29:16.974 --> 00:29:18.058 line:80%
[exclaims]

00:29:18.142 --> 00:29:21.979 line:80%
Just imagining that made me so excited.

00:29:31.113 --> 00:29:32.114 line:80%
So?

00:29:33.866 --> 00:29:34.950 line:80%
What should we do first?

00:29:37.077 --> 00:29:38.370 line:80%
[in English] Yes!

00:29:39.663 --> 00:29:40.664 line:80%
[mouthing] Unbelievable.

00:29:41.206 --> 00:29:43.959 line:80%
Then, let's take a selfie first
to celebrate this day.

00:29:44.668 --> 00:29:46.837 line:80%
Sorry, but you really shouldn't…

00:29:48.547 --> 00:29:50.799 line:80%
Was I being rude, by any chance?

00:29:51.425 --> 00:29:52.426 line:80%
Very rude.

00:29:55.971 --> 00:29:57.056 line:80%
You know,

00:29:59.099 --> 00:30:00.517 line:80%
my left side is prettier.

00:30:03.354 --> 00:30:06.231 line:80%
Then, I'll take one from the left.

00:30:06.315 --> 00:30:08.567 line:80%
One, two, three.

00:30:08.651 --> 00:30:09.860 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:30:13.697 --> 00:30:16.575 line:80%
Should we show you the story reel first?

00:30:16.659 --> 00:30:19.119 line:80%
-The video will be pretty helpful.
-Sure.

00:30:19.203 --> 00:30:21.622 line:80%
The USB is in my car,
so I'll go and get it.

00:30:26.418 --> 00:30:27.586 line:80%
[door closes]

00:30:27.670 --> 00:30:28.671 line:80%
CHARACTER "WON"

00:30:28.754 --> 00:30:29.922 line:80%
[Nana] It's strange.

00:30:30.506 --> 00:30:32.216 line:80%
-She looks familiar.
-[Ben] Pardon?

00:30:32.299 --> 00:30:35.177 line:80%
It's an original character
that Chan created.

00:30:35.260 --> 00:30:36.261 line:80%
No…

00:30:37.221 --> 00:30:38.931 line:80%
I'm sure I've seen that face before.

00:30:39.014 --> 00:30:40.015 line:80%
[elevator dings]

00:30:43.268 --> 00:30:44.603 line:80%
[humming]

00:30:47.481 --> 00:30:49.024 line:80%
[humming continues]

00:30:54.947 --> 00:30:55.948 line:80%
Hmm?

00:31:08.419 --> 00:31:09.920 line:80%
[sighs]

00:31:13.549 --> 00:31:15.551 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:31:34.820 --> 00:31:35.821 line:80%
Huh.

00:31:36.613 --> 00:31:38.615 line:80%
[footsteps echoing]

00:32:05.309 --> 00:32:06.560 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Ms. Song.</i>

00:32:06.644 --> 00:32:07.728 line:80%
Right.

00:32:07.811 --> 00:32:11.315 line:80%
This character looks like
our lead designer, Song Haran.

00:32:12.983 --> 00:32:14.568 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

00:32:24.203 --> 00:32:25.204 line:80%
[echoing] I'm sorry.

00:32:25.871 --> 00:32:28.082 line:80%
I dropped my pen by accident.

00:32:34.546 --> 00:32:35.923 line:80%
May I help you?

00:32:38.258 --> 00:32:39.259 line:80%
[echoing stops]

00:32:39.343 --> 00:32:41.387 line:80%
Are you here for the collaboration?

00:32:44.264 --> 00:32:45.265 line:80%
No…

00:32:47.768 --> 00:32:48.978 line:80%
Oh.

00:32:49.770 --> 00:32:50.771 line:80%
Yes, I am.

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:54.775 line:80%
It's nice to meet you.

00:32:55.526 --> 00:32:57.027 line:80%
I'm Song Haran, the lead designer.

00:32:57.903 --> 00:32:58.904 line:80%
[sighs]

00:32:59.655 --> 00:33:00.781 line:80%
[mutters] "It's nice to meet you"?

00:33:03.283 --> 00:33:05.577 line:80%
-Excuse me?
-Right.

00:33:07.663 --> 00:33:09.790 line:80%
It's nice to meet you.

00:33:13.460 --> 00:33:14.795 line:80%
I'm Seonu Chan.

00:33:14.878 --> 00:33:16.880 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:33:21.802 --> 00:33:22.845 line:80%
My pen…

00:33:23.679 --> 00:33:25.180 line:80%
Ah… Here.

00:33:27.975 --> 00:33:29.226 line:80%
Thank you.

00:33:39.028 --> 00:33:40.487 line:80%
Do you have something to say?

00:33:41.947 --> 00:33:42.948 line:80%
No.

00:34:08.515 --> 00:34:11.560 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

00:34:17.566 --> 00:34:18.901 line:80%
[sighs]

00:34:18.984 --> 00:34:21.570 line:20%
NANA ATELIER DESIGNERS
LEAD DESIGNER SONG HARAN

00:34:25.199 --> 00:34:26.617 line:80%
[sighs]

00:34:38.921 --> 00:34:40.130 line:80%
Hey, Chan.

00:34:40.214 --> 00:34:42.716 line:80%
-What happened to you?
-It's fine.

00:34:43.300 --> 00:34:44.301 line:80%
[knock on door]

00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:48.681 line:80%
[door closes]

00:34:49.807 --> 00:34:50.808 line:80%
[Haran] I'm sorry.

00:34:50.891 --> 00:34:52.726 line:80%
My prior engagement
ran longer than expected.

00:34:52.810 --> 00:34:53.936 line:80%
No need for excuses.

00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:55.562 line:80%
Say hello.

00:34:55.646 --> 00:34:57.147 line:80%
This is Lead Designer Song Haran,

00:34:57.231 --> 00:35:00.067 line:80%
who will be the main support
for this collaboration project.

00:35:00.150 --> 00:35:02.611 line:80%
She'll be working with you
for the entire three months.

00:35:03.696 --> 00:35:04.822 line:80%
Let's continue.

00:35:04.905 --> 00:35:06.991 line:80%
[Ben] Then,
let's watch the story reel together.

00:35:07.825 --> 00:35:09.034 line:80%
[Nana] Wait.

00:35:10.077 --> 00:35:11.745 line:80%
Mr. Seonu.

00:35:12.371 --> 00:35:13.789 line:80%
That character.

00:35:14.331 --> 00:35:15.541 line:80%
Was it based on someone?

00:35:17.292 --> 00:35:19.795 line:80%
No, it just came to mind.

00:35:19.878 --> 00:35:21.130 line:80%
My grandmother…

00:35:21.213 --> 00:35:24.258 line:80%
I mean, Ms. Kim said that
Won resembles my sister…

00:35:24.341 --> 00:35:25.467 line:80%
[groans]

00:35:25.551 --> 00:35:28.137 line:80%
I mean, Lead Designer Song Haran.

00:35:28.220 --> 00:35:29.430 line:80%
[both exclaim]

00:35:29.513 --> 00:35:30.889 line:80%
-Ooh!
-[in English] Oops.

00:35:30.973 --> 00:35:32.683 line:80%
[in Korean] I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:35:33.767 --> 00:35:34.768 line:80%
I…

00:35:36.520 --> 00:35:37.896 line:80%
I can't stand those messy clothes.

00:35:37.980 --> 00:35:40.190 line:80%
-Remy, get him a new shirt.
-[Remy] Yes, ma'am.

00:35:40.274 --> 00:35:41.734 line:80%
We'll resume in 10 minutes.

00:35:42.359 --> 00:35:44.361 line:80%
[Remy] Why don't you wait
in the fitting room?

00:35:44.445 --> 00:35:46.613 line:80%
I'll pick out a pretty shirt for you.

00:35:47.072 --> 00:35:48.240 line:80%
It's on the fourth floor.

00:35:48.324 --> 00:35:50.034 line:80%
-[Chan] I'll do it.
-[Hayeong] No, it's fine.

00:35:50.117 --> 00:35:52.202 line:80%
It's all right.
Just head to the fourth floor.

00:35:59.877 --> 00:36:01.754 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[footsteps approaching]

00:36:08.510 --> 00:36:11.513 line:80%
Can you deliver this to the animator?
[chuckles]

00:36:11.597 --> 00:36:16.393 line:80%
I mean, seeing you
brooding like this by yourself again…

00:36:16.477 --> 00:36:20.689 line:80%
You look [in English] very, very…
[in Korean] free right now. [chuckles]

00:36:22.858 --> 00:36:23.859 line:80%
[Remy chuckles]

00:36:29.615 --> 00:36:30.616 line:80%
[sighs]

00:36:30.699 --> 00:36:32.201 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:36:32.284 --> 00:36:34.286 line:80%
[♪ soft pensive music playing]

00:36:51.553 --> 00:36:53.305 line:80%
I'll leave your shirt here.

00:37:01.063 --> 00:37:02.356 line:80%
-[exclaims]
-[groans]

00:37:02.439 --> 00:37:03.941 line:80%
I'm sorry! You weren't answering.

00:37:04.024 --> 00:37:05.234 line:80%
Right.

00:37:06.777 --> 00:37:08.320 line:80%
[sighs] Ah…

00:37:10.280 --> 00:37:12.366 line:80%
Here's your shirt.

00:37:12.449 --> 00:37:13.492 line:80%
Thank you.

00:37:18.539 --> 00:37:21.125 line:80%
[sighing]

00:37:21.208 --> 00:37:23.168 line:80%
[♪ soft pensive music continuing]

00:37:26.296 --> 00:37:27.423 line:80%
[door closes]

00:37:33.762 --> 00:37:34.763 line:80%
What's with you today?

00:37:35.931 --> 00:37:37.182 line:80%
You've been acting weird…

00:37:38.350 --> 00:37:39.351 line:80%
What are you doing?

00:37:39.893 --> 00:37:42.855 line:80%
I'm sorry, Ben.
I'm stepping out of this project.

00:37:43.689 --> 00:37:44.898 line:80%
[exclaims in English] What?

00:37:44.982 --> 00:37:46.525 line:80%
[in Korean] You stick to the schedule.

00:37:46.608 --> 00:37:47.651 line:80%
I'll head back to the US.

00:37:51.613 --> 00:37:53.407 line:80%
This isn't funny, Chan.

00:37:54.450 --> 00:37:57.161 line:80%
I'll call you as soon as I find
a replacement supervisor.

00:37:58.829 --> 00:38:00.039 line:80%
What on earth…

00:38:00.122 --> 00:38:01.790 line:80%
[in English] Are you serious right now?

00:38:01.874 --> 00:38:04.960 line:80%
You know the director's coming here
with the EA team soon, right?

00:38:05.044 --> 00:38:07.838 line:80%
Hundreds of people have been working
on this project for years

00:38:07.921 --> 00:38:09.256 line:80%
because they believed in you.

00:38:09.340 --> 00:38:11.258 line:80%
Not to mention the expenses.

00:38:11.925 --> 00:38:13.344 line:80%
[in Korean] Seonu Chan.

00:38:14.887 --> 00:38:17.139 line:80%
The Seonu Chan I know wouldn't do this.

00:38:17.890 --> 00:38:19.058 line:80%
No, he can't.

00:38:20.559 --> 00:38:21.560 line:80%
Tell me the reason.

00:38:21.644 --> 00:38:23.646 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:38:24.647 --> 00:38:25.814 line:80%
Because I'm scared.

00:38:25.898 --> 00:38:26.982 line:80%
I shouldn't be here.

00:38:28.400 --> 00:38:29.652 line:80%
What do you mean?

00:38:31.362 --> 00:38:33.072 line:80%
[in English] Sorry, Ben. Not now.

00:38:33.947 --> 00:38:35.366 line:80%
Let's talk about it later, man.

00:38:43.957 --> 00:38:47.294 line:80%
[in Korean] You said
drawing made you so happy.

00:38:48.253 --> 00:38:49.797 line:80%
When you became a supervisor,

00:38:49.880 --> 00:38:52.383 line:80%
you asked me to smack you
because it felt like a dream.

00:38:53.342 --> 00:38:55.719 line:80%
[in English] Now I see
just how little it really means to you.

00:38:58.722 --> 00:38:59.723 line:80%
[in Korean] Fine. Go.

00:39:00.265 --> 00:39:03.477 line:80%
I don't need a supervisor
who gives up so easily on his work.

00:39:09.525 --> 00:39:11.026 line:80%
[door opens, closes]

00:39:12.778 --> 00:39:13.821 line:80%
[sighs]

00:39:13.904 --> 00:39:15.489 line:80%
WON COSTUME COLLABORATION PROPOSAL

00:39:17.992 --> 00:39:19.034 line:80%
[sighs]

00:39:20.661 --> 00:39:21.662 line:80%
[sighs]

00:39:31.714 --> 00:39:32.923 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:39:39.430 --> 00:39:40.472 line:80%
<i>Memento mori…</i>

00:39:47.896 --> 00:39:48.897 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:39:59.158 --> 00:40:00.617 line:80%
[ticking]

00:40:04.830 --> 00:40:06.248 line:80%
[in English] He sure left quick.

00:40:06.915 --> 00:40:08.917 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:40:10.711 --> 00:40:12.588 line:80%
<i>Morning, Ben. How are you?</i>

00:40:12.671 --> 00:40:15.257 line:80%
<i>Wait, actually. It's probably</i>
<i>nighttime there, right?</i>

00:40:15.341 --> 00:40:17.051 line:80%
-[chuckles]
<i>-Anyway, I was just wondering</i>

00:40:17.134 --> 00:40:19.678 line:80%
<i>how the first meeting went</i>
<i>for the fashion collaboration.</i>

00:40:19.762 --> 00:40:22.264 line:80%
Uh, yeah, it went well, but…

00:40:22.348 --> 00:40:27.936 line:20%
Before we get into that,
there's been a bit of an issue with Chan.

00:40:28.020 --> 00:40:31.190 line:20%
-Um…
-Hey, am I late?

00:40:32.399 --> 00:40:34.777 line:80%
Sorry. I was taking a shower.

00:40:36.236 --> 00:40:38.614 line:80%
I thought I should get dressed
before hopping on.

00:40:41.075 --> 00:40:42.493 line:80%
Let's share it.

00:40:42.993 --> 00:40:44.703 line:80%
-Okay.
-[Chan sighs]

00:40:46.288 --> 00:40:48.165 line:80%
Okay, um…

00:40:48.248 --> 00:40:50.167 line:80%
I've sent the materials to Ms. Kim,

00:40:50.250 --> 00:40:54.880 line:80%
and we're meeting in a couple of days
to discuss the concept.

00:40:54.963 --> 00:40:56.340 line:80%
[director] <i>All right. Sounds great.</i>

00:40:56.423 --> 00:40:59.426 line:80%
-Right?
-Yeah. Yeah. That's right. Uh…

00:41:01.303 --> 00:41:02.763 line:80%
-[in Korean] Seonu Chan.
-Yeah?

00:41:02.846 --> 00:41:04.431 line:80%
-What was that?
-What?

00:41:04.515 --> 00:41:05.599 line:80%
Your clothes were gone.

00:41:05.683 --> 00:41:07.726 line:80%
Oh. I dropped them off at the cleaners.

00:41:08.519 --> 00:41:09.812 line:80%
They were all crumpled.

00:41:10.354 --> 00:41:12.982 line:80%
-Let's go get some soy-marinated crabs.
-Soy-marinated crabs?

00:41:13.524 --> 00:41:14.650 line:80%
It's midnight.

00:41:14.984 --> 00:41:16.568 line:80%
[sighs]

00:41:16.652 --> 00:41:19.196 line:80%
Don't you know shops are open
24 hours a day in Korea?

00:41:20.030 --> 00:41:23.742 line:80%
We need to eat well
in order to work hard, you know.

00:41:23.826 --> 00:41:26.245 line:80%
-Right, Producer Ben?
-Seonu Chan.

00:41:27.496 --> 00:41:30.207 line:80%
-You're buying.
-No, I'm not. Last one out is buying.

00:41:32.584 --> 00:41:33.669 line:80%
[Ben exclaims]

00:41:34.753 --> 00:41:36.755 line:80%
[door opens, closes]

00:41:41.385 --> 00:41:42.720 line:80%
[sighs]

00:41:43.345 --> 00:41:44.596 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

00:41:44.680 --> 00:41:45.681 line:80%
[clicks tongue]

00:41:45.764 --> 00:41:47.057 line:80%
Three months…

00:41:48.559 --> 00:41:49.852 line:80%
Just three months.

00:41:54.315 --> 00:41:56.692 line:80%
[sighs] I'm sure nothing will happen.

00:42:01.488 --> 00:42:02.489 line:80%
[door opens]

00:42:03.198 --> 00:42:04.199 line:80%
[door closes]

00:42:04.283 --> 00:42:06.035 line:80%
-[wind whooshes]
-[papers rustling]

00:42:12.875 --> 00:42:14.209 line:20%
[camera whirring, clicking]

00:42:14.293 --> 00:42:16.295 line:20%
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

00:42:19.131 --> 00:42:21.175 line:20%
[camera clicking, whirring]

00:42:27.222 --> 00:42:28.766 line:80%
[thudding]

00:42:29.308 --> 00:42:32.102 line:80%
-[door opens, closes]
-[Hadam] Grandma.

00:42:32.186 --> 00:42:34.772 line:80%
-[Nana] Hey.
-I'm here.

00:42:34.855 --> 00:42:36.982 line:80%
How was your day?

00:42:37.066 --> 00:42:38.859 line:80%
Mmm. It was tough.

00:42:38.942 --> 00:42:42.071 line:80%
It's hard being a high school senior.

00:42:42.905 --> 00:42:44.239 line:80%
But…

00:42:46.575 --> 00:42:47.910 line:20%
Ta-da!

00:42:47.993 --> 00:42:50.079 line:20%
I got a perfect score
after all that studying.

00:42:51.080 --> 00:42:54.708 line:80%
Gosh, you did a great job. [chuckles]

00:42:54.792 --> 00:42:56.794 line:80%
These brains and these looks.

00:42:56.877 --> 00:43:00.172 line:80%
I got so many good genes
from you, Grandma.

00:43:00.255 --> 00:43:01.465 line:80%
[Nana chuckles]

00:43:02.341 --> 00:43:05.094 line:80%
But what did I say
was just as important as studying?

00:43:05.177 --> 00:43:06.637 line:80%
Managing my health.

00:43:07.262 --> 00:43:08.263 line:80%
Here.

00:43:08.764 --> 00:43:12.810 line:80%
I've been taking the tonics
that Mr. Yeon gave me to help me focus.

00:43:12.893 --> 00:43:14.603 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-I'll go get some rest.

00:43:14.687 --> 00:43:16.188 line:80%
Good night, Grandma.

00:43:16.981 --> 00:43:17.982 line:80%
Good night.

00:43:21.151 --> 00:43:22.319 line:80%
[sighs]

00:43:32.413 --> 00:43:34.415 line:80%
How are you busier
than a high school senior?

00:43:37.084 --> 00:43:38.669 line:80%
Where on earth have you…

00:43:40.921 --> 00:43:42.464 line:80%
Forget it. Go upstairs.

00:43:43.966 --> 00:43:44.967 line:80%
Good night.

00:43:52.558 --> 00:43:53.642 line:80%
[sighs]

00:43:57.104 --> 00:43:58.105 line:80%
[knock on door]

00:44:02.151 --> 00:44:04.987 line:80%
Why leave your perfectly fine room
and go into that cave?

00:44:07.406 --> 00:44:08.407 line:80%
Come to my study.

00:44:08.907 --> 00:44:09.908 line:80%
What?

00:44:09.992 --> 00:44:11.535 line:80%
Don't make me repeat myself.

00:44:11.618 --> 00:44:12.870 line:80%
Meet Photographer Yoon.

00:44:13.704 --> 00:44:15.789 line:80%
He's been interested in you
for a long time.

00:44:15.873 --> 00:44:17.958 line:80%
He's talented and has great character.

00:44:18.042 --> 00:44:20.127 line:80%
Someone like that is rare.
Give him a chance.

00:44:20.210 --> 00:44:23.339 line:80%
-No, I'm not interested in dating--
-I know.

00:44:23.839 --> 00:44:25.049 line:80%
Just change your mind.

00:44:25.841 --> 00:44:28.052 line:80%
I'll set a date, so meet with him.

00:44:31.639 --> 00:44:32.640 line:80%
[sighs]

00:44:34.058 --> 00:44:35.100 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:44:36.477 --> 00:44:39.313 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:45:07.758 --> 00:45:10.052 line:80%
FAREWELL TO MY FORMER LIFE

00:45:14.723 --> 00:45:16.350 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music continuing]

00:45:21.480 --> 00:45:22.606 line:80%
[sighs]

00:45:23.607 --> 00:45:26.151 line:80%
-[wind whooshing]
-[birds chirping]

00:45:30.114 --> 00:45:31.907 line:80%
[footsteps approaching]

00:45:33.826 --> 00:45:34.827 line:80%
[grunts]

00:45:37.538 --> 00:45:39.289 line:80%
Good morning.

00:45:39.373 --> 00:45:40.833 line:80%
"Good morning"?

00:45:40.916 --> 00:45:42.459 line:80%
When did you get home last night?

00:45:42.543 --> 00:45:45.087 line:80%
Just a little after midnight.

00:45:45.170 --> 00:45:47.172 line:80%
I suddenly got a bunch of plans.

00:45:48.549 --> 00:45:52.219 line:80%
[sighs] Why is everyone
in this household so extreme?

00:45:52.302 --> 00:45:54.096 line:80%
I wish I could mix the two of you.

00:45:54.179 --> 00:45:57.057 line:80%
-What? Me and who?
-[sighs]

00:45:57.141 --> 00:45:58.225 line:80%
[snores]

00:45:58.309 --> 00:46:00.227 line:80%
My lonely eldest sister?

00:46:01.312 --> 00:46:02.396 line:80%
[Hayeong scoffs]

00:46:02.479 --> 00:46:05.024 line:80%
[reporter]
<i>At a construction site in Seoul,</i>

00:46:05.107 --> 00:46:07.568 line:80%
<i>a large tower of scaffolding</i>

00:46:07.651 --> 00:46:09.737 line:20%
<i>begins to tilt toward the sidewalk.</i>

00:46:09.820 --> 00:46:14.283 line:20%
<i>The scaffolding was a second away</i>
<i>from falling on a woman passing by.</i>

00:46:14.366 --> 00:46:15.784 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:46:15.868 --> 00:46:17.578 line:80%
What's with all this fuss again?

00:46:17.661 --> 00:46:19.455 line:80%
[reporter continues speaking]

00:46:19.538 --> 00:46:20.539 line:80%
[TV beeps]

00:46:21.623 --> 00:46:22.833 line:80%
What are you doing?

00:46:22.916 --> 00:46:23.917 line:80%
Well…

00:46:24.335 --> 00:46:25.377 line:80%
[sighs]

00:46:26.211 --> 00:46:28.589 line:80%
I'm trying to protect

00:46:28.672 --> 00:46:32.801 line:80%
my beautiful grandmother's skin
from all the electromagnetic waves.

00:46:32.885 --> 00:46:36.138 line:80%
It's a display of touching devotion
from your second granddaughter.

00:46:36.221 --> 00:46:40.351 line:80%
[chuckles nervously]
I'll go get ready for work now.

00:46:42.603 --> 00:46:44.438 line:80%
-[thuds]
-[groans]

00:46:49.151 --> 00:46:51.111 line:80%
She still hasn't sobered up yet.

00:46:51.195 --> 00:46:52.613 line:80%
Haran!

00:46:53.656 --> 00:46:55.240 line:80%
What? Where is she?

00:46:56.283 --> 00:46:57.326 line:80%
Are you in there again?

00:46:57.409 --> 00:46:59.620 line:80%
Come out here right now!

00:47:01.330 --> 00:47:02.331 line:80%
What is it?

00:47:02.873 --> 00:47:03.916 line:80%
[whooshes]

00:47:08.504 --> 00:47:09.505 line:80%
What?

00:47:11.215 --> 00:47:15.135 line:80%
This woman passing by who almost
got hurt at a construction site.

00:47:15.219 --> 00:47:16.470 line:80%
This is you, isn't it?

00:47:16.845 --> 00:47:17.846 line:80%
It is.

00:47:18.931 --> 00:47:21.016 line:80%
-[grumbles]
-What?

00:47:21.100 --> 00:47:24.979 line:80%
Even I was startled by this.
What if Grandma had seen this?

00:47:25.062 --> 00:47:29.566 line:80%
Please, keep your head on straight
when you're outside. Okay?

00:47:29.650 --> 00:47:30.734 line:80%
I'll keep that in mind.

00:47:32.403 --> 00:47:34.113 line:80%
[Hayeong sighs]

00:47:34.196 --> 00:47:36.365 line:80%
[reporter on phone]
<i>The woman stopped just in time</i>

00:47:36.448 --> 00:47:38.033 line:80%
<i>when someone urgently called her name.</i>

00:47:41.870 --> 00:47:43.580 line:80%
<i>Fortunately, that stopped</i>

00:47:43.664 --> 00:47:45.249 line:80%
<i>-what could've been a terrible…</i>
-Hang on.

00:47:47.584 --> 00:47:48.585 line:80%
What?

00:47:49.044 --> 00:47:50.045 line:80%
This shirt…

00:47:50.129 --> 00:47:51.630 line:80%
[both exclaim]

00:47:51.714 --> 00:47:53.424 line:80%
<i>I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.</i>

00:47:54.508 --> 00:47:57.678 line:80%
Wow. If it weren't for him,
you would've been a goner.

00:47:58.387 --> 00:48:01.390 line:80%
-Hmm? That shirt…
-You recognize it too, right?

00:48:01.473 --> 00:48:05.602 line:80%
Yeah. We remember every color
and texture that people wear.

00:48:05.686 --> 00:48:06.687 line:80%
Isn't that…

00:48:07.187 --> 00:48:08.856 line:80%
the animator's shirt?

00:48:08.939 --> 00:48:11.400 line:80%
-It is. He wore it at the meeting.
-What on earth?

00:48:11.483 --> 00:48:14.278 line:80%
Then, does that mean he was passing by

00:48:14.361 --> 00:48:16.405 line:80%
and shouted when he saw
that you were in danger?

00:48:16.488 --> 00:48:18.198 line:80%
He called out my name.

00:48:18.282 --> 00:48:19.992 line:80%
That's before we even met.

00:48:20.075 --> 00:48:23.746 line:80%
What? How did he call you by your name
when he doesn't know it?

00:48:25.247 --> 00:48:27.791 line:80%
Ah. I get it.

00:48:27.875 --> 00:48:30.586 line:80%
He must be someone in the industry
who knows you.

00:48:31.587 --> 00:48:33.005 line:80%
You're known for your looks.

00:48:33.088 --> 00:48:35.966 line:80%
Plus, plenty of people
wear the same clothes.

00:48:36.550 --> 00:48:37.593 line:80%
You think so?

00:48:37.676 --> 00:48:39.678 line:80%
That's the only way it makes sense.

00:48:41.180 --> 00:48:43.724 line:80%
So who could this savior be?

00:48:44.683 --> 00:48:45.684 line:80%
Right?

00:48:46.310 --> 00:48:47.478 line:80%
Who could it be?

00:48:51.774 --> 00:48:53.317 line:80%
[Sol] Oh. Hello, Ms. Song.

00:48:54.068 --> 00:48:55.069 line:80%
[Seung-gyu] Good morning.

00:48:55.152 --> 00:48:56.528 line:80%
-[in English] Hi.
-[Remy in Korean] Hello.

00:49:02.951 --> 00:49:03.952 line:80%
[beeps]

00:49:04.787 --> 00:49:05.913 line:80%
[knock on door]

00:49:05.996 --> 00:49:07.289 line:80%
Yes?

00:49:07.373 --> 00:49:10.376 line:80%
Ms. Song, the black dress sample is here.

00:49:13.962 --> 00:49:15.297 line:80%
The measurements are perfect.

00:49:15.381 --> 00:49:16.757 line:80%
Let's see it on a mannequin…

00:49:16.840 --> 00:49:17.925 line:80%
I'll wear it.

00:49:18.008 --> 00:49:19.802 line:80%
That will be easier to check.

00:49:19.885 --> 00:49:21.512 line:80%
-Okay. Thanks.
-No problem.

00:49:24.598 --> 00:49:26.600 line:80%
WORK ORDER

00:49:27.351 --> 00:49:28.352 line:80%
Oh?

00:49:30.479 --> 00:49:31.814 line:80%
Ms. Song.

00:49:31.897 --> 00:49:33.440 line:80%
What's with this men's shirt?

00:49:33.524 --> 00:49:35.901 line:80%
Just give that to me
and change into the dress.

00:49:35.985 --> 00:49:36.986 line:80%
[Sol] Okay.

00:49:39.321 --> 00:49:40.739 line:80%
[door closes]

00:49:40.823 --> 00:49:42.825 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:49:46.662 --> 00:49:49.581 line:80%
[sighs] I'm sure it's the same shirt.

00:49:52.042 --> 00:49:54.294 line:80%
[Hayeong] <i>Plenty of people</i>
<i>wear the same clothes.</i>

00:49:56.213 --> 00:49:57.339 line:80%
[sighs]

00:50:08.350 --> 00:50:09.351 line:80%
The art exhibit.

00:50:09.435 --> 00:50:11.103 line:80%
RADIANT SEASONS

00:50:11.186 --> 00:50:14.773 line:80%
I went to the exhibit
on the day of our lookbook shoot…

00:50:17.151 --> 00:50:18.152 line:80%
It was the 16th.

00:50:19.653 --> 00:50:22.364 line:80%
<i>He was at the exhibit</i>
<i>on the same day as me.</i>

00:50:23.115 --> 00:50:24.116 line:80%
<i>Then…</i>

00:50:24.700 --> 00:50:26.785 line:80%
<i>he really was the one who called my name?</i>

00:50:27.578 --> 00:50:30.497 line:80%
SEONU CHAN

00:50:31.457 --> 00:50:32.916 line:80%
Seonu Chan.

00:50:34.543 --> 00:50:35.794 line:80%
Seonu Chan…

00:50:35.878 --> 00:50:38.047 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music continuing]

00:50:38.130 --> 00:50:39.381 line:80%
[sighs]

00:50:41.633 --> 00:50:43.302 line:80%
It doesn't ring a bell.

00:50:44.428 --> 00:50:46.764 line:80%
How did he know my name?

00:50:51.477 --> 00:50:52.519 line:80%
[sighs]

00:50:52.603 --> 00:50:54.897 line:20%
SEONU CHAN

00:50:54.980 --> 00:50:56.482 line:80%
[ice crackling]

00:51:00.569 --> 00:51:01.987 line:80%
[Haran] <i>It's nice to meet you.</i>

00:51:02.071 --> 00:51:04.657 line:80%
I'm Song Haran, the lead designer.

00:51:08.285 --> 00:51:10.829 line:80%
<i>Chan. Chan.</i>

00:51:10.913 --> 00:51:12.164 line:80%
<i>I love you.</i>

00:51:12.247 --> 00:51:13.832 line:80%
<i>I love you, Chan.</i>

00:51:13.916 --> 00:51:15.751 line:80%
[EKG beeping]

00:51:17.252 --> 00:51:18.295 line:80%
[explosion]

00:51:18.379 --> 00:51:19.505 line:80%
[gasps]

00:51:20.130 --> 00:51:22.132 line:80%
[♪ soft pensive music playing]

00:51:22.216 --> 00:51:24.802 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

00:51:39.108 --> 00:51:40.192 line:80%
[sighs]

00:51:46.782 --> 00:51:48.617 line:20%
[Remy screams]

00:51:48.701 --> 00:51:50.244 line:80%
[Sol] Ms. Song.

00:51:50.327 --> 00:51:52.871 line:80%
-Something weird was delivered to you.
-What a nutjob.

00:51:54.623 --> 00:51:58.168 line:80%
What are you going to do?
I'm the one who received this delivery.

00:51:58.252 --> 00:51:59.628 line:80%
I'm going to be traumatized

00:51:59.712 --> 00:52:02.381 line:80%
after seeing something that sickening
with my pretty eyes.

00:52:02.464 --> 00:52:04.550 line:80%
Do you have any idea
who could've done this?

00:52:04.633 --> 00:52:05.759 line:80%
Not at all.

00:52:05.843 --> 00:52:07.678 line:80%
[Sol] Did you have a bad breakup recently?

00:52:07.761 --> 00:52:10.014 line:80%
Those kind of exes turn into stalkers--

00:52:10.097 --> 00:52:13.017 line:80%
It's fine. This is a personal matter.
Please get back to work.

00:52:13.100 --> 00:52:15.936 line:80%
We don't know what these weirdos
might do if we leave them be.

00:52:16.020 --> 00:52:20.149 line:80%
He's right. A crazy stalker like this
could pop out of nowhere and do something…

00:52:20.232 --> 00:52:22.651 line:80%
Thanks for your concern,
but I'll deal with it myself.

00:52:27.156 --> 00:52:29.783 line:80%
-[Seung-gyu] We're just worried…
-[Sol] Ms. Song…

00:52:30.701 --> 00:52:32.036 line:80%
-[remote beeps]
-[Sol exclaims]

00:52:32.119 --> 00:52:34.705 line:80%
[exclaims] That darned glass.
She's always turning it…

00:52:34.788 --> 00:52:37.416 line:80%
[whimpers] My pretty hands…

00:52:37.499 --> 00:52:39.626 line:80%
What kind of crazy jerk would do this?

00:52:42.338 --> 00:52:43.964 line:80%
Hang on…

00:52:44.048 --> 00:52:46.467 line:80%
[running]

00:52:47.468 --> 00:52:48.677 line:80%
[door opens]

00:52:48.761 --> 00:52:50.971 line:80%
[Hayeong] Haran. I mean, Ms. Song
since we're at work.

00:52:51.680 --> 00:52:53.349 line:80%
The stalker who sent those photos…

00:52:53.432 --> 00:52:56.852 line:80%
Maybe it's the same guy
who called your name in the street.

00:52:58.312 --> 00:52:59.563 line:80%
Right, ma'am?

00:52:59.647 --> 00:53:01.607 line:80%
He could've been following you,

00:53:01.690 --> 00:53:04.610 line:80%
and he could've yelled your name
by accident when you were in danger.

00:53:08.113 --> 00:53:11.867 line:80%
-If you're done, get back to work.
-Work isn't important right now.

00:53:11.950 --> 00:53:13.285 line:80%
[sighs]

00:53:19.083 --> 00:53:21.919 line:80%
All right, Ms. Song.

00:53:27.675 --> 00:53:30.636 line:80%
-What are you doing?
-There's a smudge on it.

00:53:30.719 --> 00:53:31.720 line:80%
Just a second.

00:53:32.429 --> 00:53:33.472 line:80%
I'll excuse myself.

00:53:35.849 --> 00:53:36.850 line:80%
[door opens]

00:53:37.476 --> 00:53:38.602 line:80%
[door closes]

00:53:39.103 --> 00:53:40.938 line:80%
[Haran] <i>If the stalker who sent the photos</i>

00:53:41.563 --> 00:53:43.691 line:80%
<i>is the same guy who called my name…</i>

00:53:44.775 --> 00:53:45.985 line:80%
Seonu Chan?

00:53:46.068 --> 00:53:48.070 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

00:53:50.864 --> 00:53:51.907 line:80%
[soft bark]

00:53:55.452 --> 00:53:56.453 line:80%
WON CHARACTER CONCEPT

00:53:56.537 --> 00:53:58.789 line:80%
[Hayeong] <i>Ms. Kim said that</i>
<i>Won resembles my sister…</i>

00:53:58.872 --> 00:54:01.417 line:80%
<i>I mean, Lead Designer Song Haran.</i>

00:54:02.418 --> 00:54:04.712 line:80%
[Haran] <i>If the character</i>
<i>is based on the type of girl he likes,</i>

00:54:05.254 --> 00:54:08.215 line:80%
<i>maybe he saw that I looked similar</i>
<i>when he came to Korea</i>

00:54:08.298 --> 00:54:10.259 line:80%
<i>and learned my name after stalking me.</i>

00:54:11.093 --> 00:54:14.013 line:80%
<i>Then, he followed me to the art exhibit</i>
<i>and witnessed the accident.</i>

00:54:15.848 --> 00:54:18.017 line:80%
<i>I bet he didn't know</i>
<i>we'd be working together.</i>

00:54:18.934 --> 00:54:19.935 line:80%
[gasps]

00:54:20.394 --> 00:54:21.854 line:80%
<i>Is that why he reacted like that?</i>

00:54:22.438 --> 00:54:24.815 line:80%
Right.

00:54:25.524 --> 00:54:26.734 line:80%
It's…

00:54:27.985 --> 00:54:29.236 line:80%
It's nice to meet you.

00:54:29.320 --> 00:54:31.989 line:80%
[Haran] <i>It's because it wasn't</i>
<i>his first time seeing me.</i>

00:54:32.906 --> 00:54:36.076 line:80%
-[scoffs]
-Emergency ice water for you.

00:54:36.160 --> 00:54:39.830 line:80%
You seemed frustrated
about something. [chuckles]

00:54:39.913 --> 00:54:42.416 line:80%
The ice machine
stopped acting up. [chuckles]

00:54:43.167 --> 00:54:47.046 line:80%
One of my regulars who's really handy
dropped by and fixed it instantly.

00:54:47.546 --> 00:54:48.797 line:80%
Thank you.

00:54:48.881 --> 00:54:50.215 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

00:54:53.177 --> 00:54:55.012 line:80%
[Nana] <i>There's an urgent meeting</i>
<i>with a client.</i>

00:54:55.095 --> 00:54:59.099 line:80%
<i>Come to Grand Lumiere Hotel</i>
<i>by 7:00 p.m. tonight.</i>

00:55:01.935 --> 00:55:03.687 line:80%
WON CHARACTER CONCEPT

00:55:05.022 --> 00:55:06.148 line:80%
[scoffs]

00:55:07.441 --> 00:55:10.611 line:20%
"SHIM"
Coffee House

00:55:10.694 --> 00:55:12.404 line:80%
[hums, grunts]

00:55:14.073 --> 00:55:15.699 line:80%
[sighs]

00:55:17.951 --> 00:55:19.119 line:80%
[sighs]

00:55:20.120 --> 00:55:22.164 line:80%
-[customer] Hello.
-Hey!

00:55:22.247 --> 00:55:25.250 line:80%
My VVIP regular who fixed my ice machine.

00:55:25.334 --> 00:55:27.211 line:80%
Come on in. [chuckles]

00:55:27.294 --> 00:55:28.671 line:80%
[in English] Welcome.

00:55:28.754 --> 00:55:30.589 line:80%
[in Korean] Hi, Genius.

00:55:30.673 --> 00:55:32.883 line:80%
Here. Sit down.

00:55:33.384 --> 00:55:34.760 line:80%
I'll make you some coffee.

00:55:34.843 --> 00:55:36.470 line:80%
Okay. Thank you.

00:55:37.012 --> 00:55:38.013 line:80%
Genius, wait.

00:55:38.472 --> 00:55:39.473 line:80%
[whines]

00:55:42.434 --> 00:55:44.812 line:80%
[Manjae] Did you go to the art exhibit?

00:55:44.895 --> 00:55:47.272 line:80%
You said you'd go right away
when I gave you the ticket.

00:55:47.815 --> 00:55:48.816 line:80%
Uh…

00:55:49.441 --> 00:55:51.777 line:80%
Yes. Thank you for the ticket.

00:55:52.611 --> 00:55:56.490 line:80%
But for someone
who always smiles so handsomely,

00:55:57.116 --> 00:55:59.326 line:80%
why do you look so gloomy today?

00:55:59.410 --> 00:56:01.245 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-Uh… [inhales sharply]

00:56:01.328 --> 00:56:03.288 line:80%
[exclaims] Right?

00:56:03.372 --> 00:56:05.958 line:80%
I'm usually really handsome,

00:56:06.667 --> 00:56:09.878 line:80%
but I didn't get much sleep,
so I guess I look less handsome today.

00:56:10.671 --> 00:56:12.256 line:80%
Why didn't you get much sleep?

00:56:12.339 --> 00:56:14.717 line:80%
Did you have a nightmare?

00:56:14.800 --> 00:56:15.843 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:56:16.468 --> 00:56:18.095 line:80%
[breathes deeply]

00:56:19.513 --> 00:56:20.597 line:80%
[Chan] Oh.

00:56:20.681 --> 00:56:22.099 line:80%
Do you play the harmonica?

00:56:22.182 --> 00:56:23.392 line:80%
Oh, that. [chuckles]

00:56:23.976 --> 00:56:26.061 line:80%
I found it while cleaning out my clutter.

00:56:27.104 --> 00:56:30.816 line:80%
I get out of breath easily now,
so my chest hurts.

00:56:30.899 --> 00:56:32.443 line:80%
I can't play it so well anymore.

00:56:32.526 --> 00:56:34.028 line:80%
-Here.
-Thank you.

00:56:34.111 --> 00:56:37.823 line:80%
I used to play that often
in my neighborhood when I was little.

00:56:37.906 --> 00:56:39.366 line:80%
Where's your hometown?

00:56:39.450 --> 00:56:41.076 line:80%
Chuncheon.

00:56:41.160 --> 00:56:43.329 line:80%
All I did was find one old object,

00:56:43.412 --> 00:56:46.707 line:80%
but it reminded me of my old hometown

00:56:46.790 --> 00:56:48.083 line:80%
and my childhood friends.

00:56:48.167 --> 00:56:55.174 line:80%
It came with a full package
of old memories. [chuckles]

00:56:57.217 --> 00:56:59.053 line:80%
Memories…

00:56:59.636 --> 00:57:00.679 line:80%
[clicks tongue]

00:57:01.555 --> 00:57:04.433 line:80%
are kind of like sausage links.

00:57:04.516 --> 00:57:06.310 line:80%
What? Sausage links?

00:57:07.269 --> 00:57:08.270 line:80%
Yes.

00:57:09.146 --> 00:57:11.231 line:80%
Even if you think
you've forgotten everything,

00:57:11.315 --> 00:57:13.233 line:80%
recalling just one memory…

00:57:15.319 --> 00:57:17.029 line:80%
seems to bring everything else along.

00:57:17.905 --> 00:57:19.114 line:80%
Like sausage links.

00:57:25.204 --> 00:57:26.205 line:80%
Hey.

00:57:26.997 --> 00:57:28.248 line:80%
Wait just a moment.

00:57:30.668 --> 00:57:31.752 line:80%
-Okay.
-Hang on.

00:57:43.138 --> 00:57:45.265 line:80%
[creaking]

00:57:52.856 --> 00:57:56.485 line:80%
[♪ playing Baroque music, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

00:58:14.044 --> 00:58:16.088 line:80%
[♪ Baroque piano music continuing]

00:58:38.360 --> 00:58:40.237 line:80%
[lively chatter]

00:58:40.321 --> 00:58:41.947 line:80%
What kind of meeting is it?

00:58:42.031 --> 00:58:43.157 line:80%
I should at least know…

00:58:43.240 --> 00:58:45.743 line:80%
I told you I'd set you up
on a date with Photographer Yoon.

00:58:45.826 --> 00:58:46.827 line:80%
No.

00:58:49.538 --> 00:58:52.041 line:80%
If that's what this is, I'm not attending.

00:58:52.791 --> 00:58:53.792 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:58:55.002 --> 00:58:57.171 line:80%
How long do I have to see you
act like this?

00:59:02.426 --> 00:59:03.844 line:80%
It's been seven years.

00:59:03.927 --> 00:59:07.306 line:80%
Everyone gets back up and lives
after going through immense pain.

00:59:07.806 --> 00:59:09.183 line:80%
You're the only one who refuses to.

00:59:10.059 --> 00:59:13.270 line:80%
Are you going to keep running away
from everything like a coward?

00:59:15.147 --> 00:59:17.483 line:80%
You can survive
with at least one person to rely on.

00:59:17.566 --> 00:59:19.693 line:80%
But with no one, you'll crumble.

00:59:21.320 --> 00:59:25.240 line:80%
Mr. Yoon can be someone like that for you.
He's a good man, so--

00:59:25.324 --> 00:59:27.326 line:80%
I don't need a good man!

00:59:28.994 --> 00:59:30.704 line:80%
How can you…

00:59:31.288 --> 00:59:33.415 line:80%
Of all people, how can you do this to me?

00:59:35.250 --> 00:59:36.835 line:80%
I'm the one who wants to live like this.

00:59:37.378 --> 00:59:39.296 line:80%
I feel comfortable this way.

00:59:40.839 --> 00:59:44.510 line:80%
I know, okay?
I know I shouldn't live like this.

00:59:45.386 --> 00:59:48.138 line:80%
I know I'm being stupid and weird.

00:59:48.973 --> 00:59:50.224 line:80%
But…

00:59:51.600 --> 00:59:52.893 line:80%
I'm too scared.

00:59:52.977 --> 00:59:55.062 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:59:55.145 --> 00:59:59.316 line:80%
I don't want to end up
being anxious and worried every day

00:59:59.942 --> 01:00:03.529 line:80%
that something might happen
to someone I care about.

01:00:04.655 --> 01:00:06.782 line:80%
So just let me live like this.

01:00:08.409 --> 01:00:11.996 line:80%
If there's no one by my side,
at least nothing bad will happen.

01:00:14.957 --> 01:00:16.458 line:80%
[exhales shakily]

01:00:58.417 --> 01:00:59.793 line:80%
[tires screeching]

01:00:59.877 --> 01:01:01.837 line:80%
Dad! Mom!

01:01:01.920 --> 01:01:03.922 line:80%
Dad! Dad!

01:01:04.673 --> 01:01:06.717 line:80%
Dad! Mom…

01:01:06.800 --> 01:01:09.678 line:80%
Mom, get up! Mom!

01:01:09.762 --> 01:01:11.388 line:80%
Oh, my God!

01:01:11.472 --> 01:01:13.265 line:80%
Help!

01:01:13.349 --> 01:01:14.475 line:80%
No, Mom…

01:01:14.558 --> 01:01:17.353 line:80%
Mom!

01:01:18.646 --> 01:01:20.272 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

01:01:26.945 --> 01:01:27.988 line:80%
Haran.

01:01:28.072 --> 01:01:30.324 line:80%
I can't believe what happened. Hmm?

01:01:33.577 --> 01:01:34.745 line:80%
Grandma.

01:01:36.163 --> 01:01:37.665 line:80%
Mom, Dad,

01:01:38.749 --> 01:01:40.000 line:80%
and Chan…

01:01:40.959 --> 01:01:42.419 line:80%
Even Chan is gone.

01:01:44.672 --> 01:01:47.508 line:80%
Chan is dead, too. [sobbing]

01:01:54.056 --> 01:01:57.059 line:80%
Haran, let's go home. Okay?

01:01:58.227 --> 01:02:01.897 line:80%
Chan is dead too, Grandma.

01:02:04.817 --> 01:02:06.610 line:80%
Chan…

01:02:07.236 --> 01:02:09.071 line:80%
Chan is dead, too.

01:02:11.657 --> 01:02:13.325 line:80%
[crying] Grandma…

01:02:30.718 --> 01:02:31.719 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

01:02:38.767 --> 01:02:41.186 line:80%
[Nana] <i>At least show Mr. Yoon</i>
<i>some basic courtesy.</i>

01:02:43.939 --> 01:02:45.065 line:80%
[sighs]

01:02:45.149 --> 01:02:48.527 line:80%
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

01:02:48.610 --> 01:02:49.611 line:80%
[sighs]

01:02:50.779 --> 01:02:54.783 line:80%
[♪ continues playing Baroque music
on piano]

01:03:20.768 --> 01:03:21.769 line:80%
[Chan] Oh.

01:03:22.353 --> 01:03:25.105 line:80%
-I'm sorry. I played without permission.
-[exclaims]

01:03:25.189 --> 01:03:27.024 line:80%
[in English] Bravo! [chuckles]

01:03:27.608 --> 01:03:30.277 line:80%
[in Korean] Will you have
some wine with me?

01:03:33.322 --> 01:03:35.949 line:80%
There's some sediment in this wine,

01:03:36.575 --> 01:03:39.286 line:80%
so let's drink this
after it settles in a bit.

01:03:39.370 --> 01:03:40.371 line:80%
Okay.

01:03:40.954 --> 01:03:43.832 line:80%
By the way, I guess you like Bach.

01:03:43.916 --> 01:03:45.250 line:80%
No.

01:03:45.334 --> 01:03:47.711 line:80%
I just happened to hear about the song.

01:03:47.795 --> 01:03:51.715 line:80%
Someone told me it's good for insomnia.

01:03:51.799 --> 01:03:53.717 line:80%
Seeing your expression,

01:03:53.801 --> 01:03:55.803 line:80%
I'm guessing today's the kind of day

01:03:56.553 --> 01:03:59.181 line:80%
when your memories come flooding back.

01:04:00.808 --> 01:04:02.977 line:80%
From the way they're coming back to me,

01:04:04.728 --> 01:04:06.730 line:80%
I guess I haven't forgotten about them.

01:04:06.814 --> 01:04:09.400 line:80%
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]
-They were just…

01:04:10.317 --> 01:04:11.819 line:80%
buried for a while.

01:04:13.237 --> 01:04:14.613 line:80%
[Manjae] Mmm.

01:04:15.322 --> 01:04:18.993 line:80%
The thing about memories
is that sometimes…

01:04:22.121 --> 01:04:23.831 line:80%
they're really rebellious.

01:04:23.914 --> 01:04:27.793 line:80%
The more you try to forget,
the more vivid they become.

01:04:27.876 --> 01:04:32.631 line:80%
And when you want to remember,
they run away from you.

01:04:34.633 --> 01:04:36.552 line:80%
So don't strain yourself.

01:04:36.635 --> 01:04:39.513 line:80%
Just try leaving them be.

01:04:40.139 --> 01:04:44.268 line:80%
Just like this wine,
memories get cloudy if you disturb them.

01:04:44.768 --> 01:04:49.982 line:80%
But if you leave them be,
they'll eventually become clearer.

01:04:51.108 --> 01:04:52.109 line:80%
[Manjae chuckles]

01:04:53.235 --> 01:04:55.237 line:80%
[♪ soft music continuing]

01:04:55.321 --> 01:04:56.363 line:80%
[chuckles]

01:04:56.822 --> 01:04:57.823 line:80%
All right.

01:04:58.657 --> 01:05:01.994 line:80%
I'll try to just leave them be.

01:05:02.077 --> 01:05:03.203 line:80%
-Let's drink.
-Okay.

01:05:04.121 --> 01:05:05.331 line:80%
[glass clinks]

01:05:09.335 --> 01:05:10.794 line:80%
I'm sorry.

01:05:10.878 --> 01:05:15.007 line:80%
I'll talk to Ms. Kim and make sure
this mistake doesn't happen again.

01:05:15.090 --> 01:05:19.053 line:80%
I came to say that you don't have
to waste your time on me.

01:05:20.471 --> 01:05:21.472 line:80%
[Yoon] Yes, I know.

01:05:22.431 --> 01:05:25.809 line:80%
I know you don't have any feelings for me,
but I really am sincere…

01:05:25.893 --> 01:05:26.977 line:80%
Are you kidding me?

01:05:27.061 --> 01:05:30.064 line:80%
Right. I understand
you don't want to hear it.

01:05:30.147 --> 01:05:31.815 line:80%
But I really am sincere--

01:05:31.899 --> 01:05:34.318 line:80%
I'm sincerely sorry,
but something urgent came up.

01:05:34.401 --> 01:05:36.278 line:80%
-I'll get going. I'm sorry.
-Excuse me?

01:05:36.362 --> 01:05:39.156 line:80%
[stutters] Ms. Song!

01:05:56.173 --> 01:05:57.174 line:80%
What?

01:05:57.800 --> 01:05:59.009 line:80%
Why are you…

01:05:59.093 --> 01:06:01.178 line:80%
Could you say my name?

01:06:01.887 --> 01:06:04.890 line:80%
-What?
-You're the one who called my name

01:06:04.974 --> 01:06:07.559 line:80%
in front of the art museum
on the 16th, right?

01:06:09.144 --> 01:06:11.313 line:80%
I met you for the first time
a few days ago.

01:06:12.231 --> 01:06:13.899 line:80%
How long have you known me?

01:06:17.695 --> 01:06:20.489 line:80%
Tell me how you know me.

01:06:21.490 --> 01:06:23.075 line:80%
What are you hiding?

01:06:27.788 --> 01:06:29.581 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Someone I have to meet…</i>

01:06:29.665 --> 01:06:32.084 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

01:06:33.168 --> 01:06:36.046 line:80%
<i>Someone who brought me back to life</i>

01:06:37.840 --> 01:06:38.841 line:80%
<i>and seems to hold…</i>

01:06:40.092 --> 01:06:42.970 line:80%
<i>the keys to my life.</i>

01:06:44.805 --> 01:06:46.765 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song continuing]

01:06:52.646 --> 01:06:56.108 line:80%
<i>The seasons of life</i>
<i>don't always come in order.</i>

01:06:57.026 --> 01:06:59.611 line:80%
<i>Sometimes, the moment</i>
<i>you feel like it's spring,</i>

01:07:02.197 --> 01:07:05.242 line:80%
<i>a harsh winter suddenly arrives.</i>

01:07:09.038 --> 01:07:10.122 line:80%
<i>Seven years ago,</i>

01:07:12.166 --> 01:07:13.709 line:80%
<i>in the midst of my coldest winter,</i>

01:07:14.460 --> 01:07:16.920 line:80%
<i>she came into my life</i>
<i>like a warm spring breeze.</i>

01:07:17.713 --> 01:07:19.298 line:80%
<i>And now, she's here again.</i>

01:07:20.632 --> 01:07:23.302 line:80%
<i>And that day, we had no idea</i>

01:07:23.969 --> 01:07:27.389 line:80%
<i>whether our future seasons</i>
<i>would be warm like spring</i>

01:07:28.140 --> 01:07:30.809 line:80%
<i>or harsh like winter.</i>

01:07:37.816 --> 01:07:39.401 line:80%
Seonu Chan…

01:07:41.862 --> 01:07:42.905 line:80%
who are you?

01:07:45.157 --> 01:07:46.325 line:80%
[Haran] <i>I love you, Chan.</i>

01:07:48.077 --> 01:07:49.244 line:80%
<i>I love you,</i>

01:07:50.579 --> 01:07:51.789 line:80%
<i>Kang Hyeokchan.</i>

01:07:54.667 --> 01:07:56.669 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song continues]

01:07:58.504 --> 01:08:00.923 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:22.861 --> 01:08:23.862 line:80%
[song ends]

01:08:25.030 --> 01:08:28.158 line:20%
[Haran] <i>Mr. Seonu.</i>
<i>Why are you stalking me?</i>

01:08:28.242 --> 01:08:30.035 line:20%
[Chan] <i>It feels like</i>
<i>it's hard to get close to her.</i>

01:08:30.577 --> 01:08:32.955 line:20%
[Manjae] <i>She never talks about herself.</i>

01:08:33.038 --> 01:08:34.873 line:20%
[Haran] <i>How did you know</i>
<i>I don't like eggplants?</i>

01:08:34.957 --> 01:08:37.876 line:20%
<i>There's another guy who speaks like him.</i>

01:08:37.960 --> 01:08:39.336 line:20%
[Chan] <i>Why does this keep happening?</i>

01:08:39.420 --> 01:08:40.629 line:20%
<i>It's scaring me.</i>

01:08:41.005 --> 01:08:43.048 line:20%
[Haran] <i>What are you doing here?</i>

01:08:43.132 --> 01:08:44.508 line:20%
[Chan] <i>I'm going to live here.</i>

01:08:44.591 --> 01:08:47.136 line:20%
[Nana] <i>They look good together.</i>

01:08:47.219 --> 01:08:50.139 line:20%
<i>Keep an eye on Ms. Song</i>

01:08:50.222 --> 01:08:52.099 line:20%
<i>and Seonu Chan.</i>

01:08:56.353 --> 01:08:58.355 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

01:09:04.236 --> 01:09:05.237 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:09:05.321 --> 01:09:06.322 line:80%
Translated by Juyoung Park